From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OHOS PC Developer <ohpcd@example.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Jul 2026 10:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: bypass pkg-config for curses on OHOS

OHOS CI workers ship the ncurses static library (libncursesw.a) and
headers under /storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local/{include,lib} but
do NOT install a curses.pc / ncurses.pc pkg-config file. As a result
meson's dependency('curses') fails at the pkg-config stage:

  Run-time dependency curses found: NO

A first attempt used cc.find_library('ncursesw', dirs: [...]) to
bypass pkg-config. However, meson 1.11.1's compiler.find_library
compiles and links a minimal test program to verify the library, and
under Conan's isolated MesonToolchain environment the OHOS clang
default search paths do not include /storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local
(either -I or -L), so the probe fails even though libncursesw.a exists
on disk:

  ../meson.build:150:21: ERROR: C shared or static library 'ncursesw' not found

Replace dependency('curses') with a plain declare_dependency() that
injects -I and -L/-l directly into link_args / include_directories.
This mirrors the approach used by the hexcurse / fdclone / frotz /
aamath recipes (autotools -I/-L injection) but adapted for meson's
declare_dependency API. declare_dependency() returns found() == true,
so the downstream `if curses.found()` header-detection block keeps
running. Source files do not reference HAVE_NCURSES* / HAVE_CURSES*
macros, so missed cc.has_header() probes only emit warnings, not
errors.

No source code logic changes — only the dependency discovery method.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OHOS-specific path]
Signed-off-by: OHOS PC Developer <ohpcd@example.com>

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -142,7 +142,11 @@ if is_windows
         link_args: ['-L' + deps_lib_path, '-lpdcurses']
     )
 else
-    curses = dependency('curses', required : true)
+    # OHOS: libncursesw.a + headers at /storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local/{lib,include}, no curses.pc
+    curses = declare_dependency(
+        link_args: ['-L/storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local/lib', '-lncursesw'],
+        include_directories: include_directories('/storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local/include')
+    )
 endif

 # Define some curses preprocessor symbols
